{"c":[{"id":"634598eca3ed5527","sum":"B17-B21: tests and skill evals use Eager; planError needs host sentences for new codes; lease 2 GiB for swift test; one ask per form per 30 s; record last pid post (resets HIDIdleTime); pid keys skip key equivalents; host hello settings override the helper's.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"48e738e908704c4c","sum":"B17-B21: event cards judge the last finished sentence; tests use eager; Ask field takes pid-keys.swift keys. Planner asks only about named fields; planError needs host sentences for new codes. Lease 2 GiB for swift test. Skill evals: Eager + writeElsewhere at actIfApproved.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"123cc4af275a3bc3","sum":"B17-A13: event cards judge the last finished sentence; Balanced = 4 offers/hour (tests use eager); typed About values fill at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5. Ask field: keyable non-activating panel, drive with pid-keys.swift; --calendar-test without access hands off blocked tcc.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"56870ee32e779000","sum":"B17-B18: event cards judge only the last finished sentence (test bodies end with it, arrive as a change); Balanced allows 4 offers/hour (use eager); typed About values fill only when both asks call the field the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (16/20 held-out, 0 wrong).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1148a14e8f8ea414","sum":"B17 socket tests: an event card judges only the last finished sentence, so a body ends with it and arrives as a change (empty first); Balanced allows 4 offers an hour, so a test needing a fifth sends level eager first.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T191104Z-3aee21889eca1d38","text":"Event cards judge only the last finished sentence of what is typed: a test body must end with the event sentence and arrive as a change (empty body first), or no attend question is asked (B17 privacy session).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T191104Z-a560fe18d0d7ba87","text":"Balanced allows 4 offers an hour (settings.ts LEVELS): a socket test that needs a fifth pop-up sends settings level eager first, or the gate silently holds it (B17).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0bc8adb9f0371420","sum":"B17-B18: live Jev picks typed About Name/Email at 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 cutoff; prompt rewordings did not help. Such a value fills only when both asks call the field the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (held-out 16 of 20, 0 wrong).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T191104Z-ec0243a8194ed7a7","text":"Live Jev picks a typed About Name/Email in both asks but at 0.23-0.88, under the 0.75 fill cutoff, on standalone forms (B17 held-out: 1-3 of 17 filled, 0 wrong); three prompt rewordings on a dev set did not raise it (evidence/screen/b17/dev).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T203647Z-3b718a56937eb180","text":"A typed About value fills only when both asks also answer the field's whose-details question as the user's at WHOSE_CUTOFF 0.5 (fill.ts); a memory cutoff alone needed 0.6 on B18's dev set and filled 4-7 of 20, the whose question 12 of 20, held-out live 16 of 20 with 0 wrong.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"184666ae87f4b0f6","sum":"A13: ask field sits in the keyable non-activating activity panel (sendEvent takes Return/Tab/Esc/Cmd-Z); drive it with scripts/pid-keys.swift, not cua-driver. Golden line 32 now has calendar. --calendar-test without Calendar access hands off blocked tcc, no grant.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"7b00489091032a4a","sum":"A13: the ask field lives in the keyable, non-activating activity list panel, whose sendEvent intercepts Return/Tab/Esc/Cmd-Z (the field editor eats Tab and Esc first). Golden protocol line 32 now has the calendar role (b610800); HelperProtocolTests compares it as is.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T195705Z-0509a06fd894e25f","text":"Caret's ask field lives in the activity list panel (OverlayPanel keyable, non-activating); Return/Tab/Esc are intercepted in the panel's sendEvent, because the field editor eats Tab and Esc before SwiftUI onKeyPress (A13).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T195705Z-b2dcf80bc4cc0ac3","text":"helper/fixtures/golden/protocol.ndjson line 32 still holds the host's pre-calendar default roles; HelperProtocolTests compares it with calendar removed until the screen track rewrites the line (A13).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"028910e321e65bd9","sum":"A13: cua-driver background keys refuse Caret's own panels; drive the ask field with scripts/pid-keys.swift. reader --calendar-test without Calendar access ends the event run as handoff blocked tcc before any calendarGrant, so no revoke to assert.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T195705Z-c193056a6c54a222","text":"cua-driver's background press_key/type_text refuse Caret's own panels (not in the host's AXWindows: off_space_or_ax_unresolved); drive the ask field with apps/caret/scripts/pid-keys.swift (CGEventPostToPid, executable rechecked per event) (A13).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T195705Z-d51a855e42ff6461","text":"With reader --calendar-test on a Mac without Calendar access, the event run ends as handoff blocked tcc at the first calendarFind, before any calendarGrant: no grant is issued, so don't assert a revoke there (A13).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"bf77c7a094ae6b8c","sum":"B18-B21: planner asks only about named fields unless asksToFillForm; planError needs host sentences for new codes. swift test peaks <1 GB, lease 2 GiB. Skill evals need Eager + writeElsewhere at actIfApproved; undo resets clean count; planRequest.window names the window.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"87632ebd17a510aa","sum":"B18: PlanErrorCode gains need host sentences (planError is exhaustive); the planner asks only about fields the instruction names unless asksToFillForm (else nothingToDo). swift test peaks under 1 GB RSS; lease 2 GiB. Routine evals copy new values each time (B19).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8ece4134d4c0c551","sum":"B18 planner: asks only about fields the instruction names unless asksToFillForm (no field named: nothingToDo); PlanErrorCode gained wrongKind, which v2/host's exhaustive planError switch needs a sentence for.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T203647Z-c901993f6e9aca54","text":"PlanErrorCode gained wrongKind (B18, kinds.ts misfit: whole address in City, email in Phone); v2/host's AskCaret.planError switch is exhaustive and needs a sentence for it at its next merge of v2/screen.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T203647Z-d62444babaa7f479","text":"The planner asks only about fields the instruction names (relevance, or namesShortLabel for To/Cc/ID) unless asksToFillForm; an instruction that names no field, like 'msg: ...', now gets nothingToDo (B18 traded that for no unrequested writes).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7a2abedd05327146","sum":"swift test under heavy.sh peaks 0.25-0.97 GB RSS; ask the lease for 2 GiB (6 GiB is refused below ~17 GiB free). Routine evals copy new values each occurrence, or the closed destination's text is taken as the next source and predictions miss (B19).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T203647Z-db99791d758fef32","text":"swift test under heavy.sh peaks at 0.25-0.44 GB RSS (/usr/bin/time -l, B18); a 6 GiB lease estimate is refused below ~17 GiB free disk, so ask for 2 GiB.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T221243Z-01ce9c46dd16673e","text":"Routine evals must copy new values each occurrence: with static source text the closed earlier destination's recent text is credited as the next source, the shape changes and predictions miss (B19; caret-fixture --windows forms, stdin form next).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"fcfc053532a2a74e","sum":"B19: real-time skill evals need Eager and writeElsewhere at actIfApproved (a background fixture is never the user's window); fixture AX writes land in the cell. Undoing a skill run resets its clean count. planRequest.window names the reader's window (B21).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"496e4b113a33f3ef","sum":"B19: real-time skill evals need Eager (8 offers/hour) and writeElsewhere at actIfApproved, since a background fixture is never the user's window. caret-fixture AX value writes land in the cell; reformat via the cell's setters and accessibilityValue().","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T221243Z-69bacc9b74bdc91c","text":"Real-time skill evals need Helper offersPerHour (Eager allows 8 offers an hour) and writeElsewhere set to actIfApproved, since a background-only fixture is never the user's window and ask first caps promotion (B19).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T221243Z-e6e14bbcf17c1b8d","text":"caret-fixture: AX value writes land in the NSTextField's cell and AX reads return a cached value; to reformat input, override the cell's objectValue/stringValue setters and the field's accessibilityValue() -> String? (setAccessibilityValue never fires) (B19).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0904bb5ea3de3ad2","sum":"B19: undoing a skill run resets its clean count (ten more clean runs after run 11's undo); live Jev's first naming ask often misses NAME_CUTOFF, the retry picks. The host never learns the reader's windowId; planRequest.window {pid, number, title} (B21) names it.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T221243Z-e77935deee83e487","text":"Skills (B19): undoing a skill run resets its clean count, so a fixture forced-mismatch run with no Tab needs ten more clean runs after run 11's undo. Live Jev's first naming ask fell under NAME_CUTOFF 0.5 in 7 of 9 tries; the reworded retry picked.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T223314Z-4eadad36fdc3c539","text":"planRequest.windowId is the reader's '<pid>-<n>' id, which the host never learns for an arbitrary window; the host sends none until the helper's schema takes pid + window number (A14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f43181fb01fd7248","sum":"B20-B21 evals: one ask per form per 30 s; record last pid post (resets HIDIdleTime); pid keys skip key equivalents; Electron evals drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE; rebuild caret-screen after mutation tests. Host hello settings override the helper's.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c7ddae6ec9f72113","sum":"GUI evals: focus another field first (one ask per form per 30 s); record last pid post (resets HIDIdleTime); per-pid tap sees posted clicks. B20: no routine in TextEdit; Electron evals drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE; reader focuses a WebKit field before AXValue.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"06c4eb4b2069c343","sum":"GUI evals: helper asks about a form once per 30 s, so focus another field first; empty a filled form before memory-negative checks. Only a per-pid listen tap sees pid-posted clicks; pid input resets HIDIdleTime, so evals record their last post.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"11d6b8ce1c2c781d","sum":"A14 fill scripts: the helper asks about a form at most once per 30 s and refocusing a focused field posts nothing; focus another field first, start 40 s after the reader. A form the run filled is a source for the next: empty it before a memory-negative check.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T223314Z-9d4eecfc20a632d3","text":"On-screen fill scripts: the helper asks about a form at most once per 30 s (helper.ts FILL_REPEAT_MS) and refocusing an already-focused field posts no focus change; focus another field first and start 40 s after the reader (A14 memory_fill_walk.py).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T223314Z-ab5b060c9c18fb41","text":"A form the run filled is a window source for the next form: a memory-negative check must empty it first, or Jev may offer its values 'from Caret Fixture, Claim form' (A14 walk-3).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0e52faea4df6a779","sum":"B20: only a per-pid listen tap sees clicks posted to that pid; caret-fixture needs --foreground to take posted clicks. Pid-posted input resets HIDIdleTime like a person's; evals record their last post (synthetic-input.ts) or the idle gate stops them.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T234914Z-795f3dcc958c0f2c","text":"A listen-only tap per pid sees clicks posted to that pid; the global NSEvent monitor and a session tap do not (B20, 6 of 6 vs 0 of 6). A background-only caret-fixture takes no posted click and cannot hit-test a covered window; --foreground (accessory) does both.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T234914Z-993bc2a42fa75599","text":"Input posted to a pid (CGEventPostToPid) resets HIDIdleTime like a person's (B20: 196 s to 0.3 s); GUI evals that post input record their last post (helper/scripts/synthetic-input.ts) or the idle gate stops them as 'user back'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"86e4f5ca0fc2bedb","sum":"B20: no routine in TextEdit; routines place late edits from where elements were last seen (closing windows lose fields). Electron evals drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE. WKWebView non-key: AXValue hits the focused field; the reader focuses a WebKit field first.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"18fa59e7880eb67e","sum":"B20: TextEdit cannot host a routine (one text area, no positions, one value per field). A closing window can reach the model without its fields; routines place late edits and presses from where elements were last seen, or verified runs score as misses.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T234914Z-ac2ee9392ce81473","text":"TextEdit cannot host a B19 routine: a shape is (source template, part, destination template) with no positions, a document is one text area, values copied from list lines share one source template, and engine.plan writes one value per field (B20).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T004204Z-5758654235cf32d7","text":"A closing window (Chrome tearing down its page, a Send that closes it) can reach the model without its fields before its close; routines place late edits and presses from where elements were last seen, or Caret's verified runs score as misses (B20).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"33e7e4ffcec40777","sum":"B20: evals that start Electron must drop ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE (the agent host sets it). WKWebView in a non-key window applies AXValue to whichever field has focus; the reader focuses a WebKit field first (focusValue, 3/3), pid typing or paste lands 0/3.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T004204Z-584e781bcb96f4a6","text":"The agent host sets ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE for its children; an eval that starts Electron must drop it or Electron runs as plain Node and cannot require('electron') (B20).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T004204Z-9249ce81a51a9397","text":"WKWebView in a window that is not key applies an AXValue write to whichever field has focus (none: dropped; another: overwritten). The reader focuses a WebKit web field first (focusValue): 3/3 landed, no raise or activation; typing or paste to the pid land 0/3 (B20).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9ef1a1669491abb1","sum":"A15-B21: host hello settings override the helper's; offline replay counts approximate (hashed keys); planRequest window {pid,number,title} xor windowId; rebuild caret-screen after mutation tests; pid keys skip key equivalents; Permissions lists skills by wrote.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"dcfd3333f3e6c97d","sum":"A15: host's hello settings override the helper's (walks needing Eager set it on the host); line watches fall back to their drawn field. B21: shadow store hashes element keys, so offline replay counts are approximate; memory.sqlite routine rows are faithful.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d418e99a3c6ab50e","sum":"A15: the host sends its gate settings on hello, overriding the helper's; socket walks needing Eager send 'settings set level eager' to the host. Line watches fall back to their drawn field when a focused-frame read fails; surface.lineHidden names the cover.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T010257Z-b452bfae15d1e4dd","text":"A host connected to the helper sends its own gate settings on hello (B10), overriding the helper's constructor settings: a socket walk that needs Eager (routine offers after 3 sightings) sends 'settings set level eager' to the host (A15).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T010304Z-b5e36ef6f1a1befa","text":"Grammarly's ring is forgiven only against a frame: a failed focused-frame AX read (busy TextEdit) made the line watch hide Esc's stopped line as covered; watches now fall back to the field they were drawn for (A15). surface.lineHidden names the cover.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1da96dc9ac3df9d5","sum":"B21: the shadow store keeps element keys only as hashes, so offline replays (scripts/real-day-replay.ts) cannot recover templates or positions and their counts are approximate; memory.sqlite routine rows are the faithful count.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T010304Z-bc4f6fa45fbfa3dd","text":"B19 helper takes only {name} in a skill memoryRequest edit; host 'Put back on Tab' sends edit {onItsOwn:false} (host contract, Fixtures/memory.ndjson last line) and gets a refusal until the screen track adds it (A15).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T015937Z-03e29f7fee084743","text":"The shadow store keeps element keys only as hashes, so an offline replay cannot recover templates or positions; scripts/real-day-replay.ts counts are approximations both ways; memory.sqlite routine rows are the faithful count (B21).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"804af6bea0900317","sum":"B21: planRequest window is {pid, number, title} xor windowId; rebuild caret-screen after mutation tests; pid keys to an inactive app skip key equivalents. A16: Permissions lists skills by wrote, else by PermissionPolicy.skillRunsUnasked (mirrors skills.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"09ccc8ad4b5ca18a","sum":"B21: planRequest names its window by {pid, number, title} or windowId, never both (unread: unseenWindow; neither: frontmost app's last focused window). A mutation swift test rebuilds .build/debug/caret-screen; rebuild from restored source before GUI evals.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T015937Z-41933c0bb214864e","text":"planRequest names its window as window {pid, number, title} or windowId, never both; an unread one is unseenWindow; neither means the frontmost app's last focused window (ScreenModel.userWindow). v2/host's planError switch needs an unseenWindow sentence (B21).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T015937Z-53ebaedecebf757b","text":"swift test on a mutated source rebuilds .build/debug/caret-screen; rebuild from the restored source before any GUI eval runs those binaries (B21 caught it by timestamp).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8e978b49d8b0a3a4","sum":"B21: keys posted to an inactive app's pid skip AppKit key equivalents (default button 0/10, Space 5/5). A16: Permissions lists a skill under each rule in its wrote; without wrote, only where PermissionPolicy.skillRunsUnasked (mirrors skills.ts) allows.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T015937Z-ebf44f31f7890c91","text":"A key posted to a pid whose app is not active skips AppKit key equivalents: the fixture's default button never ran on posted Return or Enter (0 of 10), Space pressed a focused button 5 of 5. The reader places key presses from cached focus and default button (B21).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T030748Z-24aae3b87b1574fd","text":"Permissions page lists a skill under each write rule in its fields' 'wrote' (host contract; B19 helper stores wrote but strips it from replies); without it a skill is listed only where PermissionPolicy.skillRunsUnasked (mirrors skills.ts mayRunUnasked) allows now (A16).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1ed09fa24200e83f","sum":"B22-I1: tasks bind to their host connection; --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS; undo guarded by marks; the reader needs a 0700 socket dir and --auth-fd; paste count from clearContents(); CfT NM manifests in its profile; Cotypist takes plain Tab.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"43c6d2a280958efd","sum":"B22-B23: tasks bind to their host connection and are revoked on close, pause, stop or settings change; mutation tests use --build-path /tmp; --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS; undo is guarded by marks; the reader needs a 0700 socket dir and --auth-fd.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"be6d5b2b22a12f2f","sum":"B22: tasks bind to their host connection and are revoked on close, pause, stop or settings change; evals call helper.hostConnected(id). Mutation tests: --build-path /tmp. --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only. Press only whole SAFE_PRESSES labels.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b6ef750a1098cf99","sum":"B22: tasks bind to their host connection, revoked when it closes or on any pause, stop, take over or settings change; executor asks Helper.authorize before each act; evals call helper.hostConnected(id). Return in a field presses the default button, unreported.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"563c0e5f60870996","sum":"Return in a frontmost single-line field presses the default button (5/5), and B21's reader does not report it. B22: each consumer connection is a host session; tasks are revoked when it closes; in-process evals playing the host call helper.hostConnected(id).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T031707Z-b7d2054c5f965771","text":"AppKit presses a window's default button on Return typed into a single-line text field: frontmost fixture, Note focused, Send ran 5 of 5. B21's reader counts no Return while a text field has focus (brief), so that submit goes unreported (gui/keys-front).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150809Z-35454632bb9daf62","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the one that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id) or no skill runs on its own.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"648a97f969b90b5d","sum":"B22: any pause, stop, take over, settings/permission/skill/memory change or host disconnect revokes the act grant; the executor asks Helper.authorize before each write, press, raise and calendar add. Tasks bind to their host session; evals call helper.hostConnected(id).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150824Z-0b7169f06df102c4","text":"B22: every pause, take over, stop, Caret pause, settings/permission/skill/memory change and host disconnect revokes the act grant at once (Executor.revoke/recheck); the executor also asks Helper.authorize right before each write, press, raise and calendar add.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150829Z-581618fb20568b53","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the session that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c52def503bedc2af","sum":"B22: mutation tests use --build-path /tmp and grep 'recorded an issue'; --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only; press only whole SAFE_PRESSES labels, never in system prompts (change both lists + press-risk.json). Rig VM display is 2x pixels.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5df295da363b0505","sum":"B22: run mutation swift tests with --build-path /tmp/... and grep 'recorded an issue' (Swift Testing failures). --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only and caret-fixture pids; window ids are opaque to the helper.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150830Z-a3b40432646c1572","text":"B22: swift test --build-path /tmp/... keeps mutation runs out of .build/debug; Swift Testing marks failures 'recorded an issue', not ✘, so grep that when checking a mutation was caught.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150830Z-cd56cc67608f9643","text":"B22: --act-pids now needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only and caret-fixture pids; window ids are <pid>-<start µs>-<generation>-<n>, opaque to the helper.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6f5c7126a4148883","sum":"B22: presses only whole labels in SAFE_PRESSES/RiskTable.safePresses, never in system prompts; change both lists and press-risk.json together. Rig VM display is pixels at 2x (use 3840x2400 for panels); close fixture forms >=3 s after a routine run.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150843Z-b8f6b3671dd764ee","text":"B22: presses only whole labels in risk.ts SAFE_PRESSES / RiskTable.safePresses, never in a system prompt (subrole AXSystemDialog or AXSystemFloatingWindow, or a TCC/SecurityAgent process); change both lists and press-risk.json together.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T162636Z-ec02bde9a2237805","text":"Rig VM display file is pixels at 2x: 1920x1200 gives a 960x600-pt screen, too small for Caret's panels beside caret-fixture forms; A16's drawn walk uses 3840x2400. Close fixture forms >=3 s after a routine run or the bundle loses a copy and scores a miss.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e83cf8b9c81948e8","sum":"D2-03, T1, B23: open-time cards re-offer; compare values by .utf16; host: true hello is the host; marks and sameAs guard undo; the reader needs a 0700 socket dir and the launch secret on --auth-fd.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1009a4709e5e2f78","sum":"D2-03, T1, B23: open-time event cards re-offer under a new key; compare field values by .utf16 or digest (String == normalizes); spellchecker orthography is a starting point; only a host: true hello is the host.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"941fed9a992e38ea","sum":"D2-03/T1: an open-time event card (no AM/PM or end) is needsYou with choices and is re-offered under a new key; Swift String == is canonical equivalence, so field-value guards compare .utf16 or digests.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T153943Z-e96b8d822d84ddbb","text":"D2-03: an event card whose time is open (no AM/PM, no end) is figure needsYou with a choices block; the host's closed-line Tab sends no variants row, so the helper adds nothing and re-offers the card under a new key (offerWithdrawn reoffered).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T170510Z-7982a134da3a9b97","text":"Swift String == is canonical equivalence (precomposed é equals e+U+0301): guards comparing field values must use .utf16.elementsEqual or digests, or a normalizing app passes a mismatched write (T1 RangeEdit.verify).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6c6baac04522902d","sum":"T1/B23: NSSpellChecker's orthography is only a starting point under automatic language; only a consumer hello with host: true is the host (v2/host sends it), and in-process evals call helper.hostConnected(id).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T170510Z-ca62d5f751cbf8cc","text":"NSSpellChecker requestChecking treats the orthography option as a starting point: with the system's automatic language on, French text passes under en and tres passes under fr (T1, macOS 26.6).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171742Z-0e49751b5685c975","text":"B23: only a consumer hello with host: true counts as the host; other consumers bind their own work but keep no run with no Tab alive. v2/host must send host: true, or no skill runs on its own. In-process evals still call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c7edb83e11969db2","sum":"B23: marks and sameAs make undo refuse a replaced element; crash-recovery-eval SIGKILLs a real helper; the reader wants a 0700 socket dir, a 32-byte --auth-fd secret and a helperAuth bound to the peer pid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"200602a89c015e6e","sum":"B23: value writes carry a mark and undo sends sameAs (notSameElement unless the reader's own element; fakes in test/fake-marks.ts); crash-recovery-eval.ts SIGKILLs a real helper mid-run and its 'still running' check catches late crashes.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171742Z-101e1e3d273eec2a","text":"B23: forward value writes carry a mark and undo sends sameAs; the reader answers notSameElement unless the element at the key is the one it wrote (per app worker, gone on reader restart). Test fakes use test/fake-marks.ts; marks.replace(windowId, key) plays a replaced field.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171742Z-362dd90f069eee83","text":"B23: scripts/crash-recovery-eval.ts SIGKILLs a real helper child mid skill run while the script plays reader and host; its 'restarted helper is still running' check is what catches a crash after the last publish (an id collision did exactly that).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cf937cd80d01ef87","sum":"B23: the reader connects only to a 0700, user-owned socket directory (tests use mkdtemp dirs) and needs --auth-fd with a 32-byte secret, trusting a helper whose first line is helperAuth bound to LOCAL_PEERPID; launch.ts or Caret.app hands both the secret.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171742Z-7971f1eeb5bd9db9","text":"B23: the reader connects only to a socket whose directory is 0700 and the user's own (never /tmp itself; HelperServer chmods its dir). Tests and evals put sockets in mkdtemp directories.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171817Z-c0fbce2e0a5b8f78","text":"B23: caret-screen needs --auth-fd (32-byte secret) and trusts only a helper whose first line is helperAuth (HMAC of challenge+pid, pid = LOCAL_PEERPID). Use helper/src/launch.ts; evals pass --auth-fd 0, sendSecret(reader, s), new HelperServer(..., s).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c58fce45c153b1a3","sum":"B23-A18, W1-W2, I1: recovery.sqlite re-offers runs; VM jobs dismiss Setup Assistant; paste count from clearContents(); CfT NM manifests live in its profile; accept.ts under a held lock needs CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1; Cotypist takes plain Tab; page key in memory.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"96a472bfcc0dfd20","sum":"B23, A17, W2: interrupted runs return from recovery.sqlite with undo; VM jobs dismiss Setup Assistant; goldens by id; TextEdit empty-doc AX writes can't undo; paste count from clearContents(); hook Tab on desktop; react-select opacity waiver; CfT readable by caret-screen.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ec52037b93ae2cf4","sum":"B23/A17: recovery.sqlite re-offers interrupted runs with undo; VM jobs dismiss Setup Assistant in a loop; goldens are found by id; TextEdit AX writes into an empty document cannot be undone, a pid-posted Cmd-V can.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"685e3169c771d5b6","sum":"B23/A17: recovery.sqlite keeps sealed rows of runs under way, re-offered at start as 'Stopped when Caret restarted' with undo, and id generators skip ids in use; rig VM jobs run rig-dismiss-setup.py in a loop or Setup Assistant steals TextEdit's front.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171834Z-0d54f9ef314f8bad","text":"B23: recovery.sqlite holds sealed rows of runs under way (skill_id in clear). At start each row's skill goes back on Tab; readable rows list as 'Stopped when Caret restarted, at step N of M' with undo. Id generators skip ids in use (idTaken).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T174001Z-5299fa2e9eaa69bd","text":"A17: the rig VM can bring a Setup Assistant page to the front mid-job; jobs run RIG_BIN/rig-dismiss-setup.py in a watcher loop, or every later step loses TextEdit's foreground.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b72cc8dfd3b4c876","sum":"A17: host and helper goldens once clashed on host-memory-7 (since renumbered, find lines by id); in TextEdit an AX write into an empty document leaves Undo disabled while a pid-posted Cmd-V shows Undo Paste, and after real typing an AXSelectedText insert undoes cleanly.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T174001Z-618052a769e64342","text":"A17: host and helper goldens both used host-memory-7 (B22 offerOnItsOwn vs A16 wrote line); the host keeps the wrote line as host-memory-8, and the helper's copy still has two host-memory-7 replies.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T174001Z-c2cf5d037ade7fad","text":"A17 VM: in TextEdit an AXSelectedText or AXValue write into an empty document leaves Edit > Undo disabled, while a pid-posted Cmd-V shows Undo Paste; after real typing, an AXSelectedText insert comes off with the next Cmd-Z and the typing history survives.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c3f6ef5fb76ab8ed","sum":"A17/W2: take the paste's changeCount from clearContents(); memory_fill_walk runs on the desktop with a hook Tab; the walker waives opacity inside a visible react-select; headless CfT is readable by caret-screen --only-pids.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8283021a3d87faa0","sum":"A17: paste-then-reconcile takes Caret's changeCount from clearContents()'s return, never a later read; HID keys are VM-only and the VM has no Jev key, so memory_fill_walk runs on the desktop with CARET_A14_TAB=hook (a hook Tab skips the tap's consumed counter).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T174001Z-e18f8b63a04bb172","text":"A17: paste-then-reconcile takes Caret's own changeCount from clearContents()'s return (writing items does not move it, GeneralPasteboardTests); a count read later can adopt a user's copy and overwrite it on restore.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T180747Z-a16b7748bab5e5ec","text":"A17: HID keys are VM-only and the VM has no Jev key, so A14's memory_fill_walk runs on the desktop with CARET_A14_TAB=hook (Tab via the host's debug socket); a hook Tab does not move the event tap's consumed counter.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c4ee1efae430360c","sum":"W2: react-select zeroes its input's opacity once a value is chosen, so the walker waives opacity only inside a visible react-select box; headless Chrome for Testing registers with LaunchServices, so caret-screen --only-pids reads it (accept.ts's AXManualAccessibility check).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T181245Z-06db563b8bbd4ad9","text":"W2: react-select makes its input opacity 0 whenever a value is chosen, so the walker's opacity rule dropped it; walker.visibleReactSelect waives only opacity inside a visible react-select box.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T181245Z-2154a79bf4058057","text":"W2: headless Chrome for Testing registers with LaunchServices, so caret-screen --only-pids <pid> reads it; accept.ts uses that for the AXManualAccessibility log check (Electron fixture via helper/scripts/electron-setup.sh).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d2d6653a554f5ebe","sum":"W1, W2, A18, I1: connectNative keeps the worker alive; accept.ts needs CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 under a held lock; CfT reads NM manifests from its profile; forward new ActAnswer fields; VM replays Gemma; Cotypist takes plain Tab; page key in memory.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5654e8ebc5f675c6","sum":"W1/W2/A18: connectNative keeps the worker alive; accept.ts needs CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 under a held lock; CfT reads NM manifests from <profile>/NativeMessagingHosts; add new ActAnswer fields to result(); the VM replays Gemma outcomes recorded on the host.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"94fe59b2c6b52382","sum":"W1: an open connectNative port keeps the MV3 worker alive (360 s idle); run accept.ts with CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 under a held heavy lock; CfT with --user-data-dir reads NM manifests only from <profile>/NativeMessagingHosts; headless Chrome takes one URL.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T181245Z-2950b78a7b855fe8","text":"W1: an open connectNative port kept the MV3 worker alive through 360 s idle (same instance, CfT 154). Page acceptance: node fixtures/web-form/accept.ts; under a held heavy lock set CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 or its bridge build deadlocks.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T181245Z-9a5093647c9001cd","text":"W1: Chrome for Testing 154 with --user-data-dir reads Native Messaging manifests only from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; headless Chrome refuses more than one command-line URL; chrome.runtime.getFrameId is undefined in content scripts.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a32a16c552739e86","sum":"W2/A18: the extension worker's result() forwards only named ActAnswer fields, so a new field must be added there; the 4 GB rig VM cannot hold Gemma, so record with Caret --probe-replay on the host and replay with --test-hooks --ghost-replay.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T181245Z-d139eff429d072a1","text":"W2: the worker's result() forwards only named fields of ActAnswer; a new field (choice, attached) must be added there or it silently never reaches the helper.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T183212Z-262875c9dc398e3a","text":"The rig VM (4 GB) cannot hold the 3.4 GB Gemma file: record outcomes with Caret --probe-replay on the host and replay them in the guest with --test-hooks --ghost-replay <file> (A18).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d2b115d703f13fc2","sum":"A18/I1: Cotypist takes plain Tab on Sam's Mac; mid-line ghost text is mostly silenced and SuffixFit scores one token; the page key is derived in memory from the launch secret (no key file); golden lines 67-68 are W2's pageEngine.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e08d1ae5c480f911","sum":"A18: Cotypist on Sam's Mac takes plain Tab one word at a time (debug state lists otherTabOwners); mid-line ghost text is mostly silenced by KeyType's lowConfidenceMidLine, and SuffixFit scores only the first token after the caret (floor -7.0 nats).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T183212Z-37e231b8935fe92e","text":"Cotypist runs on Sam's Mac with its accept-partial shortcut on plain Tab (one word per press): Q1's one-word Tabs were Cotypist's, Caret's tap.consumed/offers.claimed truly 0; debug state lists otherTabOwners (A18).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T183212Z-d8342f2456ba377e","text":"Ghost text between words: KeyType's lowConfidenceMidLine silences most mid-line candidates in Caret --probe-replay; A18's SuffixFit scores only the first token after the caret (floor -7.0 nats, dev-run-3), since tokens 2-3 were near 0 for every candidate.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8a8589948371a0f4","sum":"I1: page.sock's key is HMAC(launch secret, 'caret-page-key'), held in memory (no key file since W3), with the helper's pid bound to LOCAL_PEERPID; caret-screen needs --auth-fd 0. Golden lines 60-66 are B23's, 67-68 W2's pageEngine.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T183627Z-67627518ce143f34","text":"I1: page.sock's key is HMAC(launch secret, 'caret-page-key') in <sock>.key, and the bridge requires engineWelcome.pid == LOCAL_PEERPID; main.ts starts no page.sock without --auth-fd. Since B23, anything that spawns caret-screen must pass --auth-fd 0 and a 32-byte secret on stdin.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T183627Z-707cb99ebedd3d58","text":"I1 golden order: protocol.ndjson lines 60-66 are B23's (hello/helperAuth/marks), 67-68 W2's pageEngine; tests index them 0-based in protocol.test.ts and GoldenTests.swift.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
